                            Consider a scenario where you have a list of employee names. 
                                    The goal is to find names that start with the letter "A", convert them to uppercase, and save them into a new list.
                            
                            1. The Old Way (Before Java 8 - Imperative)
                            
                            This approach requires manual iteration, a temporary list, and conditional statements.
                            java
                            import java.util.ArrayList;
                            import java.util.Arrays;
                            import java.util.List;
                            
                            public class ImperativeExample {
                                public static void main(String[] args) {
                                    List<String> employees = Arrays.asList("Alice", "Bob", "Alex", "Charlie", "Amanda");
                                    
                                    // Boilerplate: Temporary list required
                                    List<String> result = new ArrayList<>();
                                    
                                    // Imperative loop specifying "how" to process
                                    for (String name : employees) {
                                        if (name.startsWith("A")) {
                                            result.add(name.toUpperCase());
                                        }
                                    }
                                    
                                    System.out.println(result); // Output: [ALICE, ALEX, AMANDA]
                                }
                            }


